      "id": "claim_992e025809714e949a0ddaa3e301c88a",
      "statement": "Safari's lifecycle differences are recorded in ADRs that matter for extension changes: ADR 0019 extracts shared logic into @brijio/shared and adds a Safari adapter layer; ADR 0050 makes the Safari background page non-persistent (persistent false) for iOS/iPadOS App Store validation, requiring WebSocket connections, pending requests, and timers to be treated as volatile and recreated on wake; ADR 0051 splits build output into dist-ios (non-persistent) and dist-macos (persistent) from one iOS-safe source manifest; ADR 0052 persists desired connection state and reconnects on wake when the user previously chose Connect, with page-activity messages as wake hints only.",
