      "id": "claim_bc0137fc221c40f193a0680f15833f59",
      "statement": "The security/trust domain (docs/security) defines trust assumptions and guarantees constraining every other domain: the threat model covers malicious agents, compromised relays, network attackers, and malicious websites; trust boundaries place browser identity in the pairing token and agent authorization in a separate MCP auth token, minimize relay trust (routes without content inspection, E2E encryption planned), and explicitly do not assume network trust; guarantees state Brijio does not export cookies, clone sessions, or act as remote desktop software, and password fields return browser_error on fill attempts.",
